  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 6cm left simple mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue possibly representing axillary contents  The specimen is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm tan pink skin ellipse with a slightly eccentric REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm tan pink unremarkable nipple  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal diffuse dense gray white fibrotic tissue up to 40   which is predominantly localized to the upper outer quadrant  The fibrous tissue in the upper outer quadrant is sectioned to reveal focal cystic change with no apparent induration or other gross abnormality  No biopsy cavity is grossly identified  Sectioning of the presumed axillary contents reveals three lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A C  fibrous tissue in upper outer quadrant  D  additional dense fibrous tissue  remaining quadrants  E  one lymph node bisected  F  two lymph nodes  N R  additional sections of fibrous areas  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm right simple mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail designated by a black stitch  The specimen is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 4 3cm tan pink skin ellipse with a 3 5cm healed scar along the upper outer quadrant  Also noted is an eccentric unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink nipple  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular fibrous region outlined by hemorrhage consistent with a well healed biopsy site which comes to 0 2cm from the deep margin in the upper outer quadrant  Residual tumor is not grossly identified  The remaining cut surface shows diffuse dense gray white fibrotic tissue  up to 40   which is primarily localized to the upper outer quadrant  Sectioning of the axillary contents reveals three probable lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows  G I  previous biopsy site J K  representative fibrous tissue L  lymph nodes Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional left axillary lymph node  is a 0 6cm tan pink lymph node with minimal attached tan yellow fibroadipose tissue which is submitted in toto as M  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  DI TIAN  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY  , Primary.
