Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 MAY 91 ACCESSIONED ON  10 MAY 91 at 17 10 CLINICAL DATA  81 year old female with right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA   95    MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA   5    2  FIBROCYSTIC DISEASE  NOTE  Residual tumor within the biopsy cavity measures 2 0cm in greatest dimension  No vascular invasion is identified  The surgical resection margins are free of tumor  A single focus of intraductal carcinoma is present in breast tissue distal from the main tumor mass   slide I   LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 9 OUT OF 9 LYMPH NODES  SKIN  CHEST  EXCISION  DERMAL NEVUS WITH NEURATIZATION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Carolyn K  Pettit  M D  Signed On  16 MAY 91 at 18 26 Staff Pathologist  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  13 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  Negative Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 17 09     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained wit