                           BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY ADDENDUM Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 MAY 99 at 11 50     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     LYMPH NODES   SENTINEL NODE  LEFT AXILLA  AND  ADDITIONAL NODE    KERATIN POSITIVE TUMOR CELLS ARE NOT SEEN  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 19 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Sentinel Node  Left Axilla   is a blue colored lymph node with surrounding adipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm overall  the lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  The specimen is entirely frozen as FX 1  now in Cassette A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Additional Node  Left Axilla   is a fragment of adipose tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  The specimen is dissected to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm  yellow area  which is frozen as FX 2  now Cassette B  The remainder of the specimen is frozen as FX 3  now in Cassette C  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left Breast Mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm lumpectomy specimen  with a short stitch marking the superior  and a long stitch the lateral margin  The entire specimen is inked black  with the following additional colors over inked  posterior deep margin   blue  superior margin   orange  Cross sections reveal a rubbery  gritty  tan mass  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  0 5cm from the closest  posterior deep  resection margin  Representative sections are submitted  lateral to medial  SECTION CODES  D F  Lateral margin  G Q  Representative superior portion of specimen  lateral to medial  R Y  Representative inferior portion of specimen  lateral to medial  Z DD  Medial margin  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Additional Superior Medial Margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm portion of adipose tissue  entirely submitted in Cassettes EE GG  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Final Shaved Margins   are multiple fragments of adipose tissue  in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  The specimen is entirely submitted in Cassettes HH MM  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Lower Inner Margin   is a single  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  which is entirely submitted in Cassette NN  Resident  STACEY L  MIKESELL  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2and3  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  GROSS DIAGNOSIS BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA  O R  Resident  GUILLERMO J TEARNEY  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  LYMPH N