aspect and 0 9cm from the black inked posterior margin  The surrounding uninvolved parenchyma consists of tan pink to yellow lobulated unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Within the attached axillary tail  multiple lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 2 1cm in maximum dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Cavity to deep margin  D E  Adjacent indurated mass to anterior and posterior margins  F G  Uninvolved parenchyma  H  Two whole lymph nodes  I  Four whole lymph nodes  J  Five whole lymph nodes  K  One bisected lymph node  L  One bisected lymph node  which contained numerous metal clips  Q  Three whole lymph nodes Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional superficial tissue right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm unoriented  irregular tan yellow to pink lobulated fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an unremarkable cut surface  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes M O  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional right axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink lymph node with a minimum amount of attached tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The specimen is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette P  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  MJF                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   E PART C  BREAST RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Primary.
