Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 10 CLINICAL DATA  History of poorly differentiated  infiltrative ductal carcinoma on a prior incisional biopsy of a left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID TYPE  MULTIPLE FOCI  SEE NOTE  2  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  3 MULTIPLE INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS  4 FOREIGN BODY GRANT CELL REACTION  FAT NECROSIS  AND SCAR TISSUE  CONSISTENT WITH OLD BIOPSY CAVITY  B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY  DISSECTION  FIVE LYMPH NODES ARE NEGATIVE FOR TUMOR  NOTE  The resection margins are free of tumor  No infiltrating ductal carcinoma is seen in the lumpectomy specimen  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 02                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number  in two separate parts  Labeled  left breast mass  suture posterior margin  is a 11 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast lumpectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm skin ellipse that contains a linear  centrally located  3 3cm well healed scar  There is a suture in place designating the posterior surface  The specimen is oriented with the skin ellipse placed at the anterior  5 o clock position  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm white tan  firm  stellate lesion  with a central 0 1cm cystic cavity  that is located 0 6cm from the deep margin  0 4cm from the anterior surface  0 6cm from the lateral margin  1 5cm from the medial margin  5 5cm from the superior margin  and 0 6cm from the inferior margin  Surrounding the breast mass are a few focal areas of fat necrosis as well as some punctate calcifications  The remaining breast parenchyma is notable for white  rubbery  firm areas interposed with adipose tissue  Labeled  axillary lymph nodes  is a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm portion of fiberadipose tissue  with a suture designating the apex  The specimen is dissected to reveal five lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE to 2 4cm in greatest dimension  The cut surfaces range from fleshy tan to yellow  The specimens are bisected and one half of each lymph node is submitted  Section code  A superior margin  en face  B C inferior margin  en face  D medial margin  radial section  E lateral margin  radial section  F deep margin  radial section  G anterior margin  radial section  H tumor  representative section  I tumor  representative section  medial surface   J tumor  representative section  lateral surface   K tumor  representative section  L M breast parenchyma  representative section  deep and lateral surfaces   N breast parenchyma  representative section  deep surface   O breast with overlying skin  P S axillary lymph nodes  superior to inferior  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  BREAST TISSUE  LEFT  PART B  AXILLARY NODE  LEFT    report_end  , Primary.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 56 CLINICAL DATA  Status post right lumpectomy  radiation and chemotherapy treatment for infiltrating ductal carcinoma of the right breast in  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Now with an  inflammatory  recurrence in the right breast  The patient also has a history of left breast carcinoma in  REMOVED_CASE_ID  with a poorly differentiated infiltrating ductal carcinoma and positive nodes                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The carcinoma is small  approximately 0 4cm in diameter and is embedded in dense scar tissue  An intraductal tumorcomponent is not seen  All resection margins are free of tumor  There is no unequivocal lymphatic or vascular invasion  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 58                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 AUG 94 at 07 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast   is a 375 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm simple mastectomy specimen covered by a REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm triangular skin ellipse with a centrally placed 0 8cm unremarkable nipple  The breast is oriented with a short suture marking the superior and a long stitch marking the lateral skin ellipse  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan white  firm  irregular stellate mass with a central 1 5cm rock hard  tan area that extends 0 5cm deep and 3 0cm medially to the nipple  The mass extends 0 3cm to the closest deep margin  abuts the inferior margin  and to within 0 5cm from the skin and 2 0cm from the superior margin  There is an adjacent tan white  rubbery  fibrous area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm adjacent to the breast mass extending 2 0cm laterally  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  SECTION CODE  A B  mass with closest deep margin  D E  mass with closest inferior margin  F  mass with adjacent inferior margin  G  overlying skin adjacent to mass  H  more portion of section in cassette G  including deep margin  I  representative sections of superior margin  J  representative section of 