he specimen is inked  as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  Sectioning reveals a lower outer  quadrant biopsy clip within a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm area of irregular fibrosis with no  discrete tumor identified  This region is 1 4cm from the posterior margin and  2 1cm from anterior margin skin  Medial to the clip about 1 2cm away is an  ill defined region of ductular dilatation spanning REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  3 0cm  from the posterior margin and 2 5cm from the anterior margin  0 3cm medial to  that region and 1 5cm away from the clip is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm well  circumscribed  firm  white nodule  The nodule is 3 0cm from the posterior  margin and 2 5cm from the anterior margin  Specimen reviewed with Dr  Lerwill   Sections are submitted as follows      REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Clip site and surrounding region of irregular fibrosis    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior and posterior margins closest to clip site    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Ill defined region of ductular dilatation    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 4cm nodule  submitted entirely    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Anterior and posterior margins closet to the nodule     B  Labeled  right mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm mastectomy specimen  oriented by the surgeon with a long stitch designating the lateral position and  a short stitch designating the superior position  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  0 3cm skin ellipse with a nipple appears unremarkable  The specimen is inked  as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  0 3cm well defined  circumscribed  firm  white nodule in the lower inner  quadrant containing a clip  0 9cm from the posterior margin and 3 4cm from the  anterior margin  Centrally within the breast  11 0cm away from nodule  1  is  another firm  white  well circumscribed nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm REMOVED_DATE  cm from the posterior margin and 3 0cm from the anterior margin  4 0cm away  from nodule  2 is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm well defined  well circumscribed firm  nodule  A fourth nodule 1 5cm away from nodule  3 is also well circumscribed  and well defined  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  The remainder of the breast  consists of yellow fatty and white fibrous tissue  Specimen reviewed with Dr   Lerwill  Representative sections are submitted as follows  to include all  nodular foci     SECTION CODE    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The lower inner quadrant nodule  entirely submitted  with margins    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Central breast  to include nodules    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lower outer quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper outer quadrant    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Upper inner quadrant         PART A  BREAST MASTECTOMY  LEFT  PART B  BREAST MASTECTOMY  RIGHT       report_end  , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 40 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE REGION OF THE MASS  SEE NOTE  Note  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 07                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 57    REVISED REMOVED_DATE        RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  tan pink  firm mass  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a tan  firm nodule  grossly abutting the margin  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and resubmitted in cassette A  The remainder of the tissue is entirely submitted in B through E  A portion of the tissue is saved for research  Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST NODULE   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
