5mm in greatest dimension  No extracapsular extension is seen  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE  2 AND SEE NOTE  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  The involvement by high grade ductal carcinoma in situ is extensive  however  submission of further sections does not reveal any invasive ductal carcinoma in this specimen  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  2 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor size  Involving 9 of 20 blocks  Spanning at least 2 6cm  Grade  3  Calcifications  In the carcinoma in situ and in benign changes  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  The distances to all margins measures 0 2cm or greater  Stains for receptor  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Three microscopic clusters of keratin positive tumor cells   10 cells total and aggregating to   0 2mm   are seen on 2 of 3 keratin immunostained tissue levels  the tumor cells are not seen on the H E stained tissue section  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x 16 x 4 0cm simple mastectomy  containing an irregular REMOVED_DATE x 10 5cm portion of tan skin on the superficial aspect  The skin contains a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm unremarkable nipple areolar complex  The specimen is oriented with a stitch at 12 o clock  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal uniformly dense breast tissue within the central aspect of the breast  admixed with focal fatty areas  and predominantly fatty tissue around the edges of the specimen  Examination of the 12 o clock region in the upper inner quadrant reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan white to tan pink firmer nodule surrounded by fibrotic tissue  This nodule comes to 2 0cm of the posterior margin  The lateral aspect of the specimen is examined for lymph nodes  however  none are identified  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Bisected abnormal nodule  entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of rubbery fibrosis around the nodule of abnormality  in the 12 o clock to 1 o clock portion of the breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of rubbery fibrosis away from 12 o clock to 1o clock area  A 10  Representative section of fibrosis  including posterior margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch at 12 o clock  The surface of the specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x 12 0cm irregular portion of skin bearing a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm unremarkable nipple areolar complex  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal uniformly dense breast tissue in the central aspect of the specimen  with few focal fatty areas  The lateral aspect of the specimen is examined for lymph nodes  however none are identified  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative areas from inferior aspect of breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from mid portion of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from superior aspect of breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section including posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Further representative sections of inferior aspect of breast   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section including posterior margin  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink lymph node with attached fat  The node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1  now resubmitted in  RE