Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 39 CLINICAL DATA  Carcinoma on recent core biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  WITH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES  GRADE 2 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE CLOSEST MARGIN  MEDIAL   NEGATIVE FOR LYMPHATIC OR VASCULAR INVASION  2  IN SITU CARCINOMA  LOBULAR OR LOW GRADE DUCTAL  WITHIN AND ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE TUMOR  MARGINS NEGATIVE  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARGIN  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE IN 25 OF 25 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 23                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh from the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left partial mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of breast oriented with stitches  short stitch supperior  long stitch lateral   The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a tumor mass grossly approaching the medial margin  The tumor is 2 5cm in greatest diameter  Section code  A D  mass from anterior to posterior E  tumor to closest medial margin F  representative section of normal breast Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left breast tissue  additional medial margin  short stitch designating the superior margin and the long stitch designating the new medial margin   is an oriented fibrofatty portion of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned from medial to lateral  There is a white  centrally located area  primarily in the lateral portion of the specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  This area is entirely submitted in cassettes M P with a representative section of normal breast in Q  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  left axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of fibrofatty tissue  There are 24 tan  rubbery nodules ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  One half of the five largest nodules are submitted in cassettes G H and the remaining nodules are submitted in cassettes I L  Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD     IN