 for blood vessel invasion  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  THREE LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF CARCINOMA  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a  left simple mastectomy specimen  which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm and has an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 12 5cm tan white ellipse of skin  There is an attached stitch at one edge of the ellipse which is taken as the lateral  axillary  position  There is a central slightly inverted nipple and a REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm ecchymotic region located 2 0cm inferolateral to the nipple  The anterior margin is marked with blue ink and the posterior margin is marked with black ink  There is fascia and a few attached muscle fragments at the deep margin  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm firm ill defined lesion with irregular borders which is located at approximately the 4 o clock position beneath the areola  The lesion extends to 2 3cm of the deep margin and to 5 5cm of the anterior margin  There are a few hemorrhagic tracts in the lesion consistent with a prior biopsy site  The remainder of the tissue consists mainly of adipose tissue with a small amount of intervening soft  white fibrous tissue  No other masses or nodules are grossly identified  No lymph nodes are identified in the region adjacent to the stitch  Representative sections are submitted as   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tumor with posterior margin in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections away from lesion  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  axillary contents  is a 4 5x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm irregular portion of adipose tissue within which two lymph nodes are identified measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x 0 9x 0 4cm  Each node has soft tan cut surfaces and is bisected  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Smaller node bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remainder of adipose tissue  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel lymph node  are three lymph nodes  The first measures 1 7cm in greatest diameter and is bivalved and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX 1 and 1A  now  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two more lymph nodes are identified measuring 0 9cm each  Both lymph nodes are entirely submitted for frozen as FX 1B and then resubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   All the lymph nodes have firm tan  cut surfaces  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION   1 and 1A  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL   METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1B  TWO LYMPH NODES  SENTINEL   METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  Gross Dictation by Tim Robinson  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Matthew M Johnson M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  66  to chromosome 17 signals  66  in 38 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Addendum by Atul K Bhan M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
