uch clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a right mastectomy specimen measuring 22 x 18 x 4 5cm with a 12 x 5cm grossly unremarkable ellipse of skin containing a 2 x 2cm grossly unremarkable nipple areolar complex  Also included is a 7 x 4 x 1 8cm axillary content  The deep margin is inked and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm moderately well circumscribed  firm  gray nodular mass in the medial half of the specimen  this mass is 0 8cm from the deep margin which is the closest margin and more than 4cm from all the other margins  Also noted medially  1 5cm from the large nodular mass  is a 0 8cm irregular  stellate  hard white tan nodular lesion located at 2 5cm from the medial margin and 0 7cm from the deep margin  which is the closest margin   The remainder of the breast is adipose with large gray white  firm  irregular areas  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Larger mass with deep margin  B  Larger mass with deep margin  C D  Smaller mass with deep margin  E F  Representative sections from the tissue adjacent to the larger mass  G  Representative section from the medial half of the breast  H I  Representative sections from the lateral half of the breast  J  Nipple  The axillary tail contains ten lymph nodes varying from REMOVED_DATE to 0 8cm  The most proximal lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes K and L  The most distal lymph nodes are submitted in cassette M  Resident  SELIM NASSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 35 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of tumor  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is confined to the lymph node  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 59                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast with axillary contents  is a 19 x 15 x 6cm left mastectomy specimen with an 11 x 9 x 2 5cm attached axillary tail  There is an overlying 16 x 8cm skin ellipse with an eccentric  unremarkable nipple areola complex  There are no evident scars on the skin surface  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm firm  stellate  tan white tumor located 0 5cm from the closest deep margin and 0 9cm from the closest anterior margin  Adjacent to this mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm rubbery area of fibrous tissue  The remaining parenchyma is interspersed with moderate amounts of dense white fibrous tissue with no additional anomalies  SECTION CODE A C  Tumor in its entirety in relation to closest deep margin  D  Lesion with adjacent fibrous area  E  Representative of unremarkable fibrous tissue from lateral aspect  F  Fibrous tissue from central aspect  G  Fibrous tissue from medial aspect  There are two ill defined  firm areas of fibrous parenchyma in the posteromedial aspect which are submitted in cassette H  Sectioning through the axillary tag reveals multiple  pink gray lymph nodes measuring up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Representative sections of each lymph node are submitted in cassettes I through K  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HONGMEI LI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Arlan F Fuller Jr   M D  Wiley W Souba Jr   M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY , Primary_(If_case_diagnosed).
