n of ductal carcinoma in situ  lobular carcinoma in situ  and atypical ductal hyperplasia  an occult invasive carcinoma cannot be excluded  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  1 AND NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE TABLE  1   ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  MULTIFOCAL  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   HEALING BIOPSY SITE WITH ADJACENT ATYPICAL COLUMNAR CELL CHANGE HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  The foci of invasive carcinoma were not identified grossly  but appeared in 3 separately submitted sections  They are morphologically similar  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA   LEFT BREAST TUMOR SIZE  Three microscopic nodules spanning REMOVED_DATE 7cm each  GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the invasive component  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  SEE SUMMARY TABLE  2 AND NOTE   NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin help determine the extent of the metastatic carcinoma in one node and reveal an additional macrometastasis in the deeper sections of the second node  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 OF 10 LYMPH NODES  SEE SUMMARY TABLE  2   TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS  2 SUMMARY OF LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  INCLUDES SENTINEL NODES  TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  2  the two sentinel nodes   TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  12 Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0 Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases 