 underestimate the true size of the tumor  GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the mass  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  The resection margins of the specimen were inked and microscopically evaluated  C  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL TISSUE   EXCISION  1  FIBROADIPOSE TISSUE WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  D  SKIN  LEFT MASTECTOMY FLAP   EXCISION  SKIN AND SUB CUTIS WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED   E  SKIN  RIGHT MASTECTOMY FLAP   EXCISION  SKIN AND SUB CUTIS WITH NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED   By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 5 containers  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a 21 x 20 x 3 5cm skin sparing simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm nipple areolar complex with a grossly unremarkable REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm nipple  The specimen is oriented as follows by the surgeon  A suture indicates 12 o clock  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal fibrous breast parenchyma with areas of nodularity and multiple cysts up to 0 5cm in diameter  from which clear straw colored fluid is expressed  No focal lesions or abnormalities are identified  The specimen is submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the posterior portion of the specimen  including black inked posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the anterior portion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the lateral portion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the medial portion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the central portion  including areas with nodularity and cysts   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of nipple  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 3cm skin sparing simple mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm nipple areolar complex with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm nipple  The specimen is oriented by the surgeon as follows  Suture indicates 6 o clock  There is a surgical metal clip on the anterior surface of the specimen  in the 11 o clock position  7 5cm from the nipple areolar complex  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a firm  tan white lesion  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  located 4 8cm from the posterior margin and 2 6cm from the anterior margin  The remaining breast parenchyma shows fibrocystic nodularity and cysts  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm area of firm  well demarcated yellow tissue  located 3 4cm from the posterior margin and 2 5cm from the anterior margin  and 2 5cm from the previously described lesion  The specimen is submitted as follows    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entirely submitted lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Adjacent areas of nodularity and cysts  representative sections   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Area of firm yellow lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of uninvolved breast parenchyma  including posterior margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of nipple  Received in formalin  labeled  additional left breast tissue  are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  which are serially sectioned t