5   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm excisional biopsy of fibrofatty breast tissue which contains REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm tan white firm irregular stellate lesion that approaches the inked resection margin by 0 1cm  The remaining breast tissue contains mature adipose tissue and white rubbery firm tissue  A representative section of the lesion is frozen as frozen section  1  and submitted in A  Section Code  A  frozen section  1  B G  mass and adjacent resection margin  H N  grossly uninvolved parenchyma and inked margins  80  of the specimen is submitted  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Diagnosis_(only_if_excisional_biopsy).
