Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Surgical Pathology Report      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  M   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  51   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Location  PAC  Institution  MGH  Date of Operation  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 14 09  Results To   Kevin S  Hughes MD  Chien Wei Eric Liao MD  PhD    FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  RIGHT     Invasive ductal carcinoma with extensive dermal involvement     Metastatic carcinoma in 10 of 11 axillary lymph nodes and multinodular  axillary soft tissue involvement     Ductal carcinoma in situ with calcifications     Fibrocystic changes and sclerosing adenosis with calcifications     Focal areas of fibrosis in parenchyma  skin  and lymph nodes consistent with  therapy effect     See note and tables  1 and  2     NOTE  Although focal areas of fibrosis consistent with therapy effect are  present  there is abundant residual invasive carcinoma both in the parenchyma  and skin  The overall grade is 2  tubule formation   2  nuclear pleomorphism    2  mitotic activity   3   but this does not quite reflect the morphologic  heterogeneity that is present  This heterogeneity is represented by many areas  that appear grade 1  some areas that appear grade 2  and scattered areas with  poor tubule formation and high mitotic activity  which would warrant a grade of  3 if viewed in isolation  Focal tumoral necrosis and minor extracellular mucin  production are also noted       TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1  INVASIVE CARCINOMA    Tumor Size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm with multiple subcentimeter satellite nodules   Grade  2  see note above    Lymphatic Vessel Invasion  Suspicious for a focus of dermal lymphatic invasion   Blood V